provider.description:
The name of the `UrlbarProvider` that provided the selected result. The possible values are: `AboutPages`, `AliasEngines`, `Autofill`, `BookmarkKeywords`, `calculator`, `UrlbarProviderContextualSearch`, `HeuristicFallback`, `HistoryUrlHeuristic`, `InputHistory`, `UrlbarProviderInterventions`, `Omnibox`, `OpenTabs`, `Places`, `PrivateSearch`, `quickactions`, `UrlbarProviderQuickSuggest`, `RemoteTabs`, `SearchSuggestions`, `UrlbarProviderSearchTips`, `TabToSearch`, `TokenAliasEngines`, `UrlbarProviderTopSites`, `UnitConversion` and `UnifiedComplete`. If engagement_type is `drop_go` or `paste_go`, this will be null because no results are shown. And also, if selected_result is `experimental_addon`, it means that the user selected a result
 from an add-on using the urlbar experimental API. In this case,
 this will be the provider name specified by the add-on.

notifications_permission_granted.description:
True if notifications are allowed from OS settings, otherwise false.
Prior to Android 13, notifications were allowed by default;
starting with Android 13,the user must explicitly grant the permission.
